{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p1-52eed72d","text":"The user wants: add embedded map from the OSM business location and, if available, opening hours, to the demo page.

Currently `BusinessLead` doesn't store coordinates or opening hours. We parse lat/lon in `overpass_isle` for dedupe but discard them. Need to add fields:
- `enlem: f64, boylam: f64` (or Option<(f64,f64)> when missing)
- `calisma_saatleri: String` (from `opening_hours` tag)

Then demo_html includes:
1. Embedded map: OSM embed iframe `https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=<lon-delta>,<lat-delta>,<lon+delta>,<lat+delta>&layer=mapnik&marker=<lat>,<lon>`. This is the standard OSM embed (no API key). Use bbox delta ~0.004 (~400m). Also link "Haritada aç" to `https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=..&mlon=..#map=18/..`.
   Caveat: iframe loads external content — fine, page already uses Tailwind CDN. Only include map when we have coordinates (we usually do for nodes/ways with center). For elements without coords (0.0), skip.

   Should use `Option<(f64,f64)>` coordinates: `konum: Option<(f64, f64)>`. In parsing: for nodes lat/lon top-level; ways/relations center. If missing → None.

2. Opening hours: OSM `opening_hours` tag is in OSM syntax, e.g. "Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00; Sa 10:00-16:00". Displaying raw is ugly. Make a small formatter translating common patterns:
   - day abbreviations: Mo→Pzt, Tu→Sal, We→Çar, Th→Per, Fr→Cum, Sa→Cmt, Su→Paz
   - "off" → "kapalı", "24/7" → "24 saat açık", "," → ", ", ";" → " · "
   - ranges "Mo-Fr" → "Pzt-Cum"
   Keep it modest: a `calisma_saatleri_metni(ham)` function that maps day tokens and separators; if it contains complex rules (e.g., "week", "PH", "[") we can just show the original? Simpler: translate day abbreviations globally with token-aware replacement, keep rest. Also handle "24/7".

   Risk: naive replacement could mangle values. Better approach: tokenize by separators (`;`, `,`, spaces) and replace known day names/ranges. Let's implement:

   ```rust
   fn calisma_saatleri_metni(ham: &str) -> String {
       let ham = ham.trim();
       if ham.is_empty() { return String::new(); }
       if ham == "24/7" { return "24 saat açık".to_string(); }
       let metin = ham
           .replace("Mo", "Pzt").replace("Tu", "Sal").replace("We", "Çar")
           .replace("Th", "Per").replace("Fr", "Cum").replace("Sa", "Cmt").replace("Su", "Paz")
           .replace("off", "kapalı")
           .replace(";", " · ");
       metin
   }
   ```
   Order matters: "Sa" replacement after "Su"? "Su" and "Sa" distinct. But "Mo" inside other words? OSM opening_hours uses only those tokens. However "Su" would match inside "Sunday"? No, OSM uses two-letter codes. Also "Th" before "Tu"? distinct. But careful: replacing "Sa" could affect "Sa" in... no.

   Edge: "Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00" → "Pzt-Cum 09:00-18:00" ✓. "Mo-Su 10:00-22:00" → "Pzt-Paz ..." ✓. "24/7" handled. "Mo off" → "Pzt kapalı".

   Should I add a note "OSM kaydındaki saatler; doğrulayın"? The demo says data from OSM. Add small "Kaynak" line already exists. Maybe append " (OSM)"? Keep simple.

Also should the map section appear only when coordinates exist; opening hours line in contact section when present.

Where to add map: after sector section, before contact section, or inside contact section? A "Konum" section with iframe and "Yol tarifi al" link (Google/OSM). Let's add a section:

