Wait: url_encode on bbox would encode commas and minus signs → `%2C` and `-` is unreserved (not encoded) good. But embedding encoded bbox in URL is fine. Alternatively keep commas literal. url_encode leaves digits, '.', '-' and encodes ',' to %2C — OSM accepts %2C. Fine.

Note `{ad}` inside format with named arg and `{embed}`/`{link}` positional? Mixing: use named args explicitly:
```rust
format!(r##"...{ad}...{embed}...{link}..."##, ad = html_kacis(ad))
```
`embed` and `link` are in scope variables — format! captures identifiers automatically (Rust 2021 inline args), and `ad` param shadows? The parameter `ad: &str` exists, so `{ad}` would use the param (unescaped) automatically; then passing `ad = html_kacis(ad)` explicitly is a duplicate named arg error? Actually explicit named arg with same name as an in-scope variable is allowed — it overrides. But then `{embed}`/`{link}` inline capture works alongside. To avoid confusion, rename param: `fn konum_bolumu_html(isletme_adi: &str, ...)` and use `{isletme_adi}` with `let isletme_adi = html_kacis(isletme_adi);` before format.

