fn calisma_saatleri_metni(ham: &str) -> String {
    let ham = ham.trim();
    if ham.is_empty() { return String::new(); }
    if ham == "24/7" { return "24 saat açık".to_string(); }
    let cevir = |parca: &str| -> String {
        // "Mo-Fr" veya "Mo" gibi gün belirteçlerini çevir; saat ve notlara dokunma.
        let mut sonuc = parca.to_string();
        for (kisa, uzun) in [("Mo","Pzt"),("Tu","Sal"),("We","Çar"),("Th","Per"),("Fr","Cum"),("Sa","Cmt"),("Su","Paz")] {
            sonuc = sonuc.replacen(kisa, uzun, 1); // hmm still naive
        }
        sonuc
    };
    ...
}
```
Token-based: split the string into words on whitespace and punctuation boundaries. Simpler: replace day codes only when the char before/after isn't alphabetic. Implement a manual scan:

```rust
fn gun_adi_cevir(parca: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
    match parca {
        "Mo" => Some("Pzt"),
        "Tu" => Some("Sal"),
        "We" => Some("Çar"),
        "Th" => Some("Per"),
        "Fr" => Some("Cum"),
        "Sa" => Some("Cmt"),
        "Su" => Some("Paz"),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```
Then scan string chars, building words of ASCII letters, and when a word is exactly a day code, replace. Preserves "Sadece" (whole word != "Sa"). Ranges "Mo-Fr" → words "Mo", "Fr" separated by '-', both replaced → "Pzt-Cum". 

```rust
fn calisma_saatleri_metni(ham: &str) -> String {
    let ham = ham.trim();
    if ham.is_empty() { return String::new(); }
    if ham == "24/7" { return "24 saat açık".to_string(); }
    let mut cikti = String::with_capacity(ham.len());
    let mut kelime = String::new();
    let bosalt = |kelime: &mut String, cikti: &mut String| {
        if !kelime.is_empty() {
            match gun_adi_cevir(kelime) { Some(uzun) => cikti.push_str(uzun), None => cikti.push_str(kelime) }
            kelime.clear();
        }
    };
    for karakter in ham.chars() {
        if karakter.is_ascii_alphabetic() {
            kelime.push(karakter);
        } else {
            bosalt(&mut kelime, &mut cikti);
            cikti.push(karakter);
        }
    }
    bosalt(&mut kelime, &mut cikti);
    cikti.replace(";", " · ").replace("off", "kapalı")
}
```
Careful: "off" appears as a word; replace word-wise too? After day conversion, "off" is a word of ASCII letters, gun_adi_cevir returns None → pushed as "off". Then `.replace("off","kapalı")` could corrupt "office"? opening_hours won't have "office". Acceptable, but do it word-wise for cleanliness: map "off" → "kapalı" in the same word function:

```rust
fn kelime_cevir(kelime: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
    match kelime {
        "Mo" => Some("Pzt"), ..., "off" => Some("kapalı"),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```
Then only separators replace `;` with " · ". Good.

