fn saat_dakika(metin: &str) -> Option<u32> {
    let (saat, dakika) = metin.split_once(':')?;
    let saat: u32 = saat.trim().parse().ok()?;
    let dakika: u32 = dakika.trim().parse().ok()?;
    if saat > 24 || dakika > 59 { return None; }
    Some(saat * 60 + dakika)
}

fn gun_indeksi(kod: &str) -> Option<usize> {
    match kod {
        "Mo" => Some(0), "Tu" => Some(1), "We" => Some(2), "Th" => Some(3),
        "Fr" => Some(4), "Sa" => Some(5), "Su" => Some(6),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```

Main parse:
```rust
fn haftalik_program(ham: &str) -> Option<[Vec<(u32, u32)>; 7]> {
    let ham = ham.trim();
    if ham.is_empty() { return None; }
    let mut program: [Vec<(u32,u32)>; 7] = Default::default();

    // "24/7" tek başına her gün 00:00-24:00
    if ham == "24/7" {
        for gun in program.iter_mut() { gun.push((0, 1440)); }
        return Some(program);
    }

    for kural in ham.split(';') {
        let kural = kural.trim();
        if kural.is_empty() { continue; }
        // Tırnak içi notları ve desteklenmeyen ifadeleri atla.
        if kural.contains('"') || kural.contains("PH") || kural.contains("week")
            || kural.contains("sunrise") || kural.contains("sunset") || kural.contains("||") {
            return None;
        }
        let parcalar: Vec<&str> = kural.split_whitespace().collect();
        // Gün kısmı opsiyonel; saat kısmı her zaman son parça.
        let (gunler, saat_metni) = match parcalar.len() {
            1 => (vec![0,1,2,3,4,5,6], parcalar[0]),
            2 => (gun_listesi(parcalar[0])?, parcalar[1]),
            _ => return None,
        };
        if saat_metni == "off" || saat_metni == "closed" {
            continue; // kapalı: aralık ekleme
        }
        let mut araliklar = Vec::new();
        for aralik in saat_metni.split(',') {
            let (bas, son) = aralik.split_once('-')?;
            let bas = saat_dakika(bas)?;
            let son = saat_dakika(son)?;
            if bas == son { return None; }
            araliklar.push((bas, son));
        }
        for gun in &gunler {
            for &(bas, son) in &araliklar {
                if bas < son {
                    program[*gun].push((bas, son));
                } else {
                    // Gece yarısını aşan aralık
                    program[*gun].push((bas, 1440));
                    program[(*gun + 1) % 7].push((0, son));
                }
            }
        }
    }
    if program.iter().all(|gun| gun.is_empty()) { return None; }
    Some(program)
}
```

gun_listesi:
```rust
fn gun_listesi(metin: &str) -> Option<Vec<usize>> {
    let mut gunler = Vec::new();
    for parca in metin.split(',') {
        if let Some((bas, son)) = parca.split_once('-') {
            let bas = gun_indeksi(bas)?;
            let son = gun_indeksi(son)?;
            let mut g = bas;
            loop {
                gunler.push(g);
                if g == son { break; }
                g = (g + 1) % 7;
                if gunler.len() > 7 { return None; }
            }
        } else {
            gunler.push(gun_indeksi(parca)?);
        }
    }
    if gunler.is_empty() { None } else { Some(gunler) }
}
```

Issue: OSM often includes rules like "Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00; Sa 10:00-16:00; Su off" — "Su off" parsed: days=["Su"], saat "off" → continue (closed). Good.

Also `Mo-Su 00:00-24:00` → bas 0, son 1440, bas<son → push. Good.

Also strings like "09:00-18:00" (no days) → len 1 → all days. Good.

Unsupported values like "Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00, Sa 09:00-13:00" (comma-separated rules without semicolon) — "saat_metni" = "09:00-18:00," etc. splitting by comma gives an empty token → parse fails → None. Acceptable (fallback: no indicator).

Also handle "Mo-Fr 09:00-12:00,13:00-18:00" → split by comma → two ranges; good.

But the split_whitespace approach breaks when rule is "Mo-Fr 09:00-12:00, 13:00-18:00" (space after comma) → 3 parts → None. Acceptable.

Also some use "Mo-Fr 9:00-18:00" single digit hour → parse ok.

Also "Mo-Su" with no time and no "off": e.g. "Mo-Su" alone → len 1, saat_metni "Mo-Su" → split '-' → saat_dakika fails → None. Fine.

What about "24/7" appearing inside e.g. "24/7" only handled exact. "Mo-Su 00:00-24:00" works.

